{"title":"Landau's Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>Landau's Problems</b> is 4 famous problems in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Number_theory\" title=\"Number theory\">Number theory</a> that number theorists had attempted to solve for centuries and failed. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"History\">History</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Landau%27s_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: History\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In 1912, famous number theorist Edmund Landau described these problems as \"unattackable by the present state of science\" in his speech at the International Congress of Mathematicians. This is where the name originated.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Problems\">The Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Landau%27s_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: The Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The problems consist of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Twin_Prime_Conjecture\" title=\"Twin Prime Conjecture\">Twin Prime Conjecture</a>, the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Goldbach_Conjecture\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Goldbach Conjecture\">Goldbach Conjecture</a>, the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=N-squared_plus_1_conjecture\" title=\"N-squared plus 1 conjecture\">n-squared plus 1 conjecture</a>, and the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Legendre_Conjecture\" title=\"Legendre Conjecture\">Legendre Conjecture</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Landau%27s_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Twin_Prime_Conjecture\" title=\"Twin Prime Conjecture\">Twin Prime Conjecture</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Goldbach_Conjecture\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Goldbach Conjecture\">Goldbach Conjecture</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=N-squared_plus_1_conjecture\" title=\"N-squared plus 1 conjecture\">n-squared plus 1 conjecture</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Legendre_Conjecture\" title=\"Legendre Conjecture\">Legendre Conjecture</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Landau%27s_Problems&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018092945\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.015 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 20/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 300/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.070      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    6.070      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:30400:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018092945 and revision id 238217. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}